WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:04.548
Welcome to Tale — and
welcome to this series.

2
00:00:04.548 --> 00:00:09.264
This first episode is the quick
tour: we’ll walk the workspace together,

3
00:00:09.264 --> 00:00:14.308
one area at a time, and you’ll watch it
answer a real question along the way.

4
00:00:14.308 --> 00:00:16.470
Here’s where we start — the chat.

5
00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:23.619
Before we type anything, take
a second to read the sidebar.

6
00:00:23.619 --> 00:00:27.589
Chat at the top — then
projects, agents, automations,

7
00:00:27.589 --> 00:00:30.510
and the knowledge your company runs on.

8
00:00:30.510 --> 00:00:34.480
Every stop on today’s tour
is one click in this rail.

9
00:00:37.180 --> 00:00:39.853
You can ask the model anything here.

10
00:00:39.853 --> 00:00:44.606
The real power is asking about
your own work — so let’s do that.

11
00:00:44.606 --> 00:00:50.250
We attach a company document as
context… the Q2 support review… and ask what

12
00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:53.592
customers said about
onboarding last quarter.

13
00:00:53.592 --> 00:00:54.260
And send.

14
00:00:56.460 --> 00:00:58.394
Now watch what comes back.

15
00:00:58.394 --> 00:01:02.410
First, the model’s
reasoning — how it plans to answer.

16
00:01:02.410 --> 00:01:05.162
Then the answer itself, streaming in.

17
00:01:05.162 --> 00:01:09.252
And read the last line: it
names the documents it used.

18
00:01:09.252 --> 00:01:10.590
Keep that in mind.

19
00:01:13.090 --> 00:01:14.936
Here’s why that matters.

20
00:01:14.936 --> 00:01:19.166
Without your documents, a
model still answers — fluent,

21
00:01:19.166 --> 00:01:21.550
confident, and sometimes wrong.

22
00:01:21.550 --> 00:01:24.088
It has never seen your customers.

23
00:01:24.088 --> 00:01:30.010
Grounded like this, every claim traces
back to a file you can open and check.

24
00:01:32.710 --> 00:01:37.983
The answer cited the Q2 support
review — so let’s find that exact file.

25
00:01:37.983 --> 00:01:43.108
We open Knowledge in the sidebar…
and there it is, indexed and ready.

26
00:01:43.108 --> 00:01:48.530
Everything in this library, your
agents can search and cite the same way.

27
00:01:51.030 --> 00:01:54.294
Next question: who answered us just now?

28
00:01:54.294 --> 00:01:59.516
We open Agents… the Chat folder…
and here it is — the Assistant.

29
00:01:59.516 --> 00:02:03.759
An agent is AI with a job
description: instructions,

30
00:02:03.759 --> 00:02:07.431
a model, tools, and the
knowledge it may use.

31
00:02:07.431 --> 00:02:10.532
Build it once; the whole team uses it.

32
00:02:13.032 --> 00:02:17.754
Agents can also work while
nobody’s watching — that’s automations.

33
00:02:17.754 --> 00:02:23.692
We open the catalog: ready-made bundles,
like syncing a mailbox or resolving GitHub

34
00:02:23.692 --> 00:02:24.392
issues.

35
00:02:24.392 --> 00:02:30.044
One of them came with this workspace —
task triage — and it’s been running this

36
00:02:30.044 --> 00:02:30.632
whole time.

37
00:02:34.332 --> 00:02:36.937
Here’s its journal: one run per row.

38
00:02:36.937 --> 00:02:42.148
Each row shows what triggered it and
how it ended — this red one failed,

39
00:02:42.148 --> 00:02:43.089
and says why.

40
00:02:43.089 --> 00:02:47.142
And before a run may send
anything out of the workspace,

41
00:02:47.142 --> 00:02:49.965
it has to wait for a person’s approval.

42
00:02:49.965 --> 00:02:52.932
Episode five opens this page up properly.

43
00:02:57.032 --> 00:03:00.141
Now, where does the
team see all this work?

44
00:03:00.141 --> 00:03:01.009
In Projects.

45
00:03:01.009 --> 00:03:05.926
This board is the website
relaunch: tasks moving from To do to Done,

46
00:03:05.926 --> 00:03:10.842
owners on the cards — your people
and your agents on the same board.

47
00:03:14.842 --> 00:03:16.368
Last stop: Settings.

48
00:03:16.368 --> 00:03:22.624
You choose which AI providers run your
requests — and which region your data stays

49
00:03:22.624 --> 00:03:23.324
in.

50
00:03:23.324 --> 00:03:27.978
And under Governance, the audit
log: every action lands here,

51
00:03:27.978 --> 00:03:29.720
with a name and a time on it.

52
00:03:32.320 --> 00:03:33.756
And that’s the tour.

53
00:03:33.756 --> 00:03:37.275
You asked a question
grounded in a real document,

54
00:03:37.275 --> 00:03:41.871
found that document in the
library, met the agent that answered,

55
00:03:41.871 --> 00:03:44.241
and read an automation’s journal.

56
00:03:44.241 --> 00:03:48.120
From here, every episode
takes one area and goes deep.

57
00:03:50.120 --> 00:03:55.256
Next time: chat, properly —
attachments, choosing the right model,

58
00:03:55.256 --> 00:03:57.279
and research with sources.

59
00:03:57.279 --> 00:04:01.481
Everything you saw today is
in the docs, page by page.

60
00:04:01.481 --> 00:04:03.272
See you in episode two.

